--| Deduction based on reductio ad absurdum. See ~ pm2.01 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 9-Feb-2017.)
theorem pm2_01da (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wn ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ps) $;

--| Deduction based on reductio ad absurdum. See ~ pm2.18 . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 9-Feb-2017.)
theorem pm2_18da (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ps $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduce an equivalence from two implications. Variant of ~ impbid . (Contributed by NM, 17-Feb-2007.)
theorem impbida (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Eliminate an antecedent implied by each side of a biconditional. Variant of ~ pm5.21ndd . (Contributed by NM, 20-Nov-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Nov-2013.)
theorem pm5_21nd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi th (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Conjunctive detachment. Theorem *3.35 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. Variant of ~ pm2.27 . (Contributed by NM, 14-Dec-2002.)
theorem pm3_35 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wi ph ps)) ps $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction form). Variant of ~ pm5.74d . (Contributed by NM, 4-May-2007.)
theorem pm5_74da (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $;

--| Theorem *4.22 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. ~ bitri in closed form. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem bitr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wb ph ps) (wb ps ch)) (wb ph ch) $;

--| A transitive law of equivalence. Compare Theorem *4.22 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1993.)
theorem biantr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wb ph ps) (wb ch ps)) (wb ph ch) $;

--| Theorem *4.14 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. Related to ~ con34b . (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Oct-2012.)
theorem pm4_14 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi (wa ph (wn ch)) (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *3.37 (Transp) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Oct-2012.)
theorem pm3_37 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi (wa ph (wn ch)) (wn ps)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedents and consequents of two premises. This is the closed theorem form of ~ anim12d . Theorem *3.47 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. It was proved by Leibniz, and it evidently pleased him enough to call it _praeclarum theorema_ (splendid theorem). (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem anim12 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ch th)) (wi (wa ph ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Conjunction implies implication. Theorem *3.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 31-Jul-1995.)
theorem pm3_4 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Inference form of ~ exbir . This proof is ~ exbiriVD automatically translated and minimized. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 31-Dec-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 27-Jan-2013.)
theorem exbiri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th ch)) $;

--| Elimination of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_61ian (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wn ph) ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ps ch $;

--| Elimination of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_61dan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Elimination of two antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jul-2013.)
theorem pm2_61ddan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wn ps) (wn ch))) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Elimination of two antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jul-2013.)
theorem pm2_61dda (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| A modus tollens deduction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 19-Aug-2009.)
theorem mtand (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ps) $;

--| Deduction for proof by contradiction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Jun-2014.)
theorem pm2_65da (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ps) $;

--| Proof by contradiction. (Contributed by NM, 9-Feb-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Jun-2014.)
theorem condan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| An implication is equivalent to the equivalence of some implied equivalence and some other equivalence involving a conjunction. A utility lemma as illustrated in ~ biadanii and ~ elelb . (Contributed by BJ, 4-Mar-2023.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 8-Mar-2023.)
theorem biadan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wb (wi ps (wb ph ch)) (wb ph (wa ps ch))) $;

--| Inference associated with ~ biadan . (Contributed by BJ, 4-Mar-2023.)
theorem biadani (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wi ps (wb ph ch)) (wb ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Alternate proof of ~ biadani not using ~ biadan . (Contributed by BJ, 4-Mar-2023.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem biadaniALT (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wi ps (wb ph ch)) (wb ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Inference associated with ~ biadani . Add a conjunction to an equivalence. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 20-Jun-2011.) (Proof shortened by BJ, 4-Mar-2023.)
theorem biadanii (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps (wb ph ch) $ >
  $ wb ph (wa ps ch) $;

--| Deduction associated with ~ biadani . Add a conjunction to an equivalence. (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 16-Jun-2024.)
theorem biadanid (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ch th)) $;

--| Two propositions are equivalent if they are both true. Theorem *5.1 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 21-May-1994.)
theorem pm5_1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ph ps) $;

--| Two propositions are equivalent if they are both false. Theorem *5.21 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 21-May-1994.)
theorem pm5_21 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wn ph) (wn ps)) (wb ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *5.35 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. Closed form of ~ 2thd . (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_35 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) (wi ph (wb ps ch)) $;

--| Introduce one conjunct as an antecedent to the other. "abai" stands for "and, biconditional, and, implication". (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Dec-2012.)
theorem abai (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph ps) (wa ph (wi ph ps)) $;

--| Conjunction with implication. Compare Theorem *4.45 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 17-May-1998.)
theorem pm4_45im (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ph (wi ps ph)) $;

--| An implication and its reverse are equivalent exactly when both operands are equivalent. The right hand side resembles that of ~ dfbi2 , but ` <-> ` is a weaker operator than ` /\ ` . Note that an implication and its reverse can never be simultaneously false, because of ~ pm2.521 . (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 18-Dec-2023.)
theorem impimprbi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb ph ps) (wb (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph)) $;

--| Theorem to move a conjunct in and out of a negation. (Contributed by NM, 9-Nov-2003.)
theorem nan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wn (wa ps ch))) (wi (wa ph ps) (wn ch)) $;

--| Theorem *5.31 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_31 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ch (wi ph ps)) (wi ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Variant of ~ pm5.31 . (Contributed by Rodolfo Medina, 15-Oct-2010.)
theorem pm5_31r (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ch (wi ph ps)) (wi ph (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.15 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 18-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm4_15 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wa ph ps) (wn ch)) (wi (wa ps ch) (wn ph)) $;

--| Theorem *5.36 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_36 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wb ph ps)) (wa ps (wb ph ps)) $;

--| A conjunction with a negated conjunction. (Contributed by AV, 8-Mar-2022.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 1-Apr-2022.)
theorem annotanannot (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wn (wa ph ps))) (wa ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.33 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_33 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wi ps ch)) (wa ph (wi (wa ph ps) ch)) $;

--| Syllogism combined with contraction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 1-Aug-2009.)
theorem syl12anc (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Syllogism combined with contraction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 1-Aug-2009.)
theorem syl21anc (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Syllogism combined with contraction. (Contributed by NM, 11-Mar-2012.)
theorem syl22anc (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ps ch) (wa th ta)) et $ >
  $ wi ph et $;

--| Four-hypothesis elimination deduction for an assertion with a singleton virtual hypothesis collection. Similar to ~ syl112anc except the unification theorem uses left-nested conjunction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.)
theorem syl1111anc (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta) et $ >
  $ wi ph et $;

--| Stacked hypotheseis implies goal. (Contributed by Stanislas Polu, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem syldbl2 (ph ps th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.)
theorem mpsyl4anc (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi th ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) ta) et $ >
  $ wi th et $;

--| Theorem *4.87 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Eric Schmidt, 26-Oct-2006.)
theorem pm4_87 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wa (wa (wb (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi ph (wi ps ch))) (wb (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ps (wi ph ch)))) (wb (wi ps (wi ph ch)) (wi (wa ps ph) ch)) $;

--| Removal of conjunct from one side of an equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.)
theorem bimsc1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wb ch (wa ps ph))) (wb ch ph) $;

--| Deduction distributing a conjunction as embedded antecedent. (Contributed by AV, 25-Oct-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Jan-2020.)
theorem a2and (ph ps ch th ta rh: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps rh) (wi ta th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps rh) ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi (wa ps ch) ta) (wi (wa ps rh) th)) $;

--| Deduction deriving nested implications from conjunctions. (Contributed by AV, 21-Aug-2022.)
theorem animpimp2impd (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (wa ps ph) (wi ch (wi th et)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ph th)) (wi et ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ps ch) (wi ps (wi th ta))) $;

--| Extend wff definition to include disjunction ("or").
term wo (ph ps: wff): wff;

--| Define disjunction (logical "or"). Definition of [Margaris] p. 49. When the left operand, right operand, or both are true, the result is true; when both sides are false, the result is false. For example, it is true that ` ( 2 = 3 \/ 4 = 4 ) ` ( ~ ex-or ). After we define the constant true ` T. ` ( ~ df-tru ) and the constant false ` F. ` ( ~ df-fal ), we will be able to prove these truth table values: ` ( ( T. \/ T. ) <-> T. ) ` ( ~ truortru ), ` ( ( T. \/ F. ) <-> T. ) ` ( ~ truorfal ), ` ( ( F. \/ T. ) <-> T. ) ` ( ~ falortru ), and ` ( ( F. \/ F. ) <-> F. ) ` ( ~ falorfal ). Contrast with ` /\ ` ( ~ df-an ), ` -> ` ( ~ wi ), ` -/\ ` ( ~ df-nan ), and ` \/_ ` ( ~ df-xor ). (Contributed by NM, 27-Dec-1992.)
axiom df_or (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Theorem *4.64 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_64 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wn ph) ps) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *4.66 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_66 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wn ph) (wn ps)) (wo ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *2.53 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_53 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.54 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_54 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wn ph) ps) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Implication in terms of disjunction. Theorem *4.6 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.)
theorem imor (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wo (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Infer disjunction from implication. (Contributed by NM, 12-Mar-2012.)
theorem imori (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wo (wn ph) ps $;

--| Infer implication from disjunction. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem imorri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wn ph) ps $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Theorem *4.62 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_62 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wn ps)) (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) $;

--| Inference disjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Apr-1994.)
theorem jaoi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch ps $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ch) ps $;

--| Add a disjunct in the antecedent of an implication. (Contributed by Rodolfo Medina, 24-Sep-2010.)
theorem jao1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps (wi ch ph) $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi ch ph) $;

--| Deduction disjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1994.)
theorem jaod (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wo ps th) ch) $;

--| Eliminate a disjunction in a deduction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 29-May-2016.)
theorem mpjaod (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Infer implication from disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 11-Jun-1994.)
theorem ori (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wn ph) ps $;

--| Infer disjunction from implication. (Contributed by NM, 11-Jun-1994.)
theorem orri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) ps $ >
  $ wo ph ps $;

--| Deduce disjunction from implication. (Contributed by NM, 27-Nov-1995.)
theorem orrd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wn ps) ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $;

--| Deduce implication from disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1994.)
theorem ord (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wn ps) ch) $;

--| Deduction introducing a disjunct. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jan-2008.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Nov-2012.)
theorem orci (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wo ph ps $;

--| Deduction introducing a disjunct. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jan-2008.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Nov-2012.)
theorem olci (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wo ps ph $;

--| Introduction of a disjunct. Theorem *2.2 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.)
theorem orc (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ph ps) $;

--| Introduction of a disjunct. Axiom *1.3 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 96. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.)
theorem olc (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ph) $;

--| Axiom *1.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 96. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm1_4 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wo ps ph) $;

--| Commutative law for disjunction. Theorem *4.31 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 15-Nov-2012.)
theorem orcom (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ps) (wo ps ph) $;

--| Commutation of disjuncts in consequent. (Contributed by NM, 2-Dec-2010.)
theorem orcomd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ch ps) $;

--| Commutation of disjuncts in antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 2-Dec-2012.)
theorem orcoms (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wo ps ph) ch $;

--| Deduction introducing a disjunct. A translation of natural deduction rule ` \/ ` IR ( ` \/ ` insertion right), see ~ natded . (Contributed by NM, 20-Sep-2007.)
theorem orcd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $;

--| Deduction introducing a disjunct. A translation of natural deduction rule ` \/ ` IL ( ` \/ ` insertion left), see ~ natded . (Contributed by NM, 11-Apr-2008.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Oct-2013.)
theorem olcd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ch ps) $;

--| Deduction eliminating disjunct. _Notational convention_: We sometimes suffix with "s" the label of an inference that manipulates an antecedent, leaving the consequent unchanged. The "s" means that the inference eliminates the need for a syllogism ( ~ syl ) -type inference in a proof. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1994.)
theorem orcs (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Deduction eliminating disjunct. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Oct-2013.)
theorem olcs (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ps ch $;

--| A lemma for Conjunctive Normal Form unit propagation, in deduction form. (Contributed by Giovanni Mascellani, 15-Sep-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Apr-2024.)
theorem olcnd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Obsolete version of ~ olcnd as of 13-Apr-2024. (Contributed by Giovanni Mascellani, 15-Sep-2017.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem unitreslOLD (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| A lemma for Conjunctive Normal Form unit propagation, in deduction form. (Contributed by Giovanni Mascellani, 15-Sep-2017.)
theorem orcnd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ps) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| A modus tollens deduction involving disjunction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 15-Jul-2009.)
theorem mtord (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wn ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wo ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn ps) $;

--| Infer negated disjunction of negated premises. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem pm3_2ni (ph ps: wff):
  $ wn ph $ >
  $ wn ps $ >
  $ wn (wo ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.45 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_45 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wn ph) $;

--| Theorem *2.46 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_46 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wn ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.47 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_47 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wo (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.48 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_48 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wo ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *2.49 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_49 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) $;

--| If neither of two propositions is true, then these propositions are equivalent. (Contributed by BJ, 26-Apr-2019.)
theorem norbi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) (wb ph ps) $;

--| If two propositions are not equivalent, then at least one is true. (Contributed by BJ, 19-Apr-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Jan-2020.)
theorem nbior (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wb ph ps)) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Elimination of disjunction by denial of a disjunct. Theorem *2.55 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jul-2012.)
theorem orel1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wi (wo ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.25 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_25 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo ph (wi (wo ph ps) ps) $;

--| Elimination of disjunction by denial of a disjunct. Theorem *2.56 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Apr-2013.)
theorem orel2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wi (wo ps ph) ps) $;

--| Slight generalization of Theorem *2.67 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_67_2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wo ph ch) ps) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.67 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_67 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wo ph ps) ps) (wi ph ps) $;

--| A non-intuitionistic positive statement, sometimes called a paradox of material implication. Sometimes called Curry's axiom. Similar to ~ exmid (obtained by substituting ` F. ` for ` ps ` ) but positive. For another non-intuitionistic positive statement, see ~ peirce . (Contributed by BJ, 4-Apr-2021.)
theorem curryax (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo ph (wi ph ps) $;

--| Law of excluded middle, also called the principle of _tertium non datur_. Theorem *2.11 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. It says that something is either true or not true; there are no in-between values of truth. This is an essential distinction of our classical logic and is not a theorem of intuitionistic logic. In intuitionistic logic, if this statement is true for some ` ph ` , then ` ph ` is decidable. (Contributed by NM, 29-Dec-1992.)
theorem exmid (ph: wff):
  $ wo ph (wn ph) $;

--| Law of excluded middle in a context. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 9-Feb-2017.)
theorem exmidd (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *2.1 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm2_1 (ph: wff):
  $ wo (wn ph) ph $;

--| Theorem *2.13 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_13 (ph: wff):
  $ wo ph (wn (wn (wn ph))) $;

--| Theorem *2.621 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_621 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wo ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.62 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Dec-2013.)
theorem pm2_62 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wi ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.68 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_68 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) ps) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Logical 'or' expressed in terms of implication only. Theorem *5.25 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-2004.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Oct-2012.)
theorem dfor2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ps) (wi (wi ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.07 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_07 (ph: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ph ph) $;

--| Axiom *1.2 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 96, which they call "Taut". (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm1_2 (ph: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ph) ph $;

--| Idempotent law for disjunction. Theorem *4.25 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 11-May-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 16-Apr-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 10-Mar-2013.)
theorem oridm (ph: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ph) ph $;

--| Theorem *4.25 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_25 (ph: wff):
  $ wb ph (wo ph ph) $;

--| Theorem *2.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_4 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wo ph ps)) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.41 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_41 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ps (wo ph ps)) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Disjoin antecedents and consequents of two premises. (Contributed by NM, 6-Jun-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jul-2012.)
theorem orim12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ch) (wo ps th) $;

--| Introduce disjunct to both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 6-Jun-1994.)
theorem orim1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch) $;

--| Introduce disjunct to both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 6-Jun-1994.)
theorem orim2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wo ch ph) (wo ch ps) $;

--| Alternate proof of ~ orim12d which does not depend on ~ df-an . This is an illustration of the conservativity of definitions (definitions do not permit to prove additional theorems whose statements do not contain the defined symbol). (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 8-Aug-2022.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem orim12dALT (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wo ps th) (wo ch ta)) $;

--| Inference adding a left disjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 12-Dec-2012.)
theorem orbi2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wo ch ph) (wo ch ps) $;

--| Inference adding a right disjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.)
theorem orbi1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch) $;

--| Infer the disjunction of two equivalences. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.)
theorem orbi12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb (wo ph ch) (wo ps th) $;

--| Deduction adding a left disjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.)
theorem orbi2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wo th ps) (wo th ch)) $;

--| Deduction adding a right disjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.)
theorem orbi1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wo ps th) (wo ch th)) $;

--| Theorem *4.37 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem orbi1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Deduction joining two equivalences to form equivalence of disjunctions. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.)
theorem orbi12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wo ps th) (wo ch ta)) $;

--| Axiom *1.5 (Assoc) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 96. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm1_5 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wo ps ch)) (wo ps (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Swap two disjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Nov-2012.)
theorem or12 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph (wo ps ch)) (wo ps (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Associative law for disjunction. Theorem *4.33 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 26-Jun-2011.)
theorem orass (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.31 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_31 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wo ps ch)) (wo (wo ph ps) ch) $;

--| Theorem *2.32 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 105. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_32 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.3 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wo ps ch)) (wo ph (wo ch ps)) $;

--| A rearrangement of disjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-1995.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 26-Jun-2011.)
theorem or32 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo (wo ph ch) ps) $;

--| Rearrangement of 4 disjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.)
theorem or4 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo ph ps) (wo ch th)) (wo (wo ph ch) (wo ps th)) $;

--| Rearrangement of 4 disjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-2005.)
theorem or42 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo ph ps) (wo ch th)) (wo (wo ph ch) (wo th ps)) $;

--| Distribution of disjunction over disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 25-Feb-1995.)
theorem orordi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph (wo ps ch)) (wo (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Distribution of disjunction over disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 25-Feb-1995.)
theorem orordir (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Disjunction distributes over implication. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jan-2013.)
theorem orimdi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.76 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_76 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.85 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm2_85 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) (wo ph (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.75 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm2_75 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wo ph (wi ps ch)) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Implication distributes over disjunction. Theorem *4.78 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm4_78 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) (wi ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| A disjunction with a true formula is equivalent to that true formula. (Contributed by NM, 23-May-1999.)
theorem biort (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ph (wo ph ps)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its disjunction with falsehood. Theorem *4.74 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 23-Mar-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 18-Nov-2012.)
theorem biorf (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb ps (wo ph ps)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its negated disjunction with falsehood. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jul-2012.)
theorem biortn (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wo (wn ph) ps)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its disjunction with falsehood. (Contributed by NM, 23-Mar-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Jul-2021.)
theorem biorfi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wn ph $ >
  $ wb ps (wo ps ph) $;

--| Theorem *2.26 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. See ~ pm2.27 . (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm2_26 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wn ph) (wi (wi ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.63 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_63 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wo (wn ph) ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *2.64 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 107. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_64 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wo ph (wn ps)) ph) $;

--| Theorem *2.42 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_42 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo (wn ph) (wi ph ps)) (wi ph ps) $;

--| A general instance of Theorem *5.11 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_11g (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wo (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ch) $;

--| Theorem *5.11 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_11 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Theorem *5.12 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_12 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.14 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_14 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wo (wi ph ps) (wi ps ch) $;

--| Theorem *5.13 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 123. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm5_13 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph) $;

--| Theorem *5.55 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm5_55 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wb (wo ph ps) ph) (wb (wo ph ps) ps) $;

--| Implication in terms of biconditional and disjunction. Theorem *4.72 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 30-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm4_72 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wb ps (wo ph ps)) $;

--| Simplify an implication between implications. (Contributed by Paul Chapman, 17-Nov-2012.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Apr-2013.)
theorem imimorb (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wi ps ch) (wi ph ch)) (wi ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Absorption of disjunction into equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 6-Aug-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Nov-2013.)
theorem oibabs (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wo ph ps) (wb ph ps)) (wb ph ps) $;

--| Disjunction distributes over the biconditional. An axiom of system DS in Vladimir Lifschitz, "On calculational proofs" (1998), ~ http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.25.3384 . (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Feb-2013.)
theorem orbidi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph (wb ps ch)) (wb (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Disjunction distributes over the biconditional. Theorem *5.7 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. This theorem is similar to ~ orbidi . (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 21-Jun-2005.)
theorem pm5_7 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wb (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch)) (wo ch (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Inference conjoining and disjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 30-Sep-1999.)
theorem jaao (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ta ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) (wi (wo ps ta) ch) $;

--| Inference disjoining and conjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by Stefan Allan, 1-Nov-2008.)
theorem jaoa (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ta ch) $ >
  $ wi (wo ph th) (wi (wa ps ta) ch) $;

--| Inference disjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 23-Oct-2005.)
theorem jaoian (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa th ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wo ph th) ps) ch $;

--| Deduction disjoining the antecedents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 14-Oct-2005.)
theorem jaodan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wo ps th)) ch $;

--| Eliminate a disjunction in a deduction. A translation of natural deduction rule ` \/ ` E ( ` \/ ` elimination), see ~ natded . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 29-May-2016.)
theorem mpjaodan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Theorem *3.44 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Oct-2013.)
theorem pm3_44 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ps ph) (wi ch ph)) (wi (wo ps ch) ph) $;

--| Disjunction of antecedents. Compare Theorem *3.44 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 5-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Apr-2013.)
theorem jao (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wi ch ps) (wi (wo ph ch) ps)) $;

--| Disjunction of antecedents. Compare Theorem *4.77 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 30-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 9-Dec-2012.)
theorem jaob (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wo ph ch) ps) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ch ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.77 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_77 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wi ps ph) (wi ch ph)) (wi (wo ps ch) ph) $;

--| Theorem *3.48 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 114. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1997.)
theorem pm3_48 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ch th)) (wi (wo ph ch) (wo ps th)) $;

--| Disjoin antecedents and consequents in a deduction. See ~ orim12dALT for a proof which does not depend on ~ df-an . (Contributed by NM, 10-May-1994.)
theorem orim12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wo ps th) (wo ch ta)) $;

--| Disjoin antecedents and consequents in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 23-Apr-1995.)
theorem orim1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wo ps th) (wo ch th)) $;

--| Disjoin antecedents and consequents in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 23-Apr-1995.)
theorem orim2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wo th ps) (wo th ch)) $;

--| Axiom *1.6 (Sum) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 97. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem orim2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.38 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 105. (Contributed by NM, 6-Mar-2008.)
theorem pm2_38 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi (wo ps ph) (wo ch ph)) $;

--| Theorem *2.36 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 105. (Contributed by NM, 6-Mar-2008.)
theorem pm2_36 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi (wo ph ps) (wo ch ph)) $;

--| Theorem *2.37 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 105. (Contributed by NM, 6-Mar-2008.)
theorem pm2_37 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi (wo ps ph) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.81 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_81 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps (wi ch th)) (wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wo ph ch) (wo ph th))) $;

--| Theorem *2.8 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm2_8 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph ps) (wi (wo (wn ps) ch) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.73 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_73 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.74 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem pm2_74 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ph) (wi (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.82 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_82 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wo (wo ph ps) ch) (wi (wo (wo ph (wn ch)) th) (wo (wo ph ps) th)) $;

--| Theorem *4.39 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_39 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wb ph ch) (wb ps th)) (wb (wo ph ps) (wo ch th)) $;

--| Conjunction implies disjunction with one common formula (1/4). (Contributed by BJ, 4-Oct-2019.)
theorem animorl (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wo ph ch) $;

--| Conjunction implies disjunction with one common formula (2/4). (Contributed by BJ, 4-Oct-2019.)
theorem animorr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wo ch ps) $;

--| Conjunction implies disjunction with one common formula (3/4). (Contributed by BJ, 4-Oct-2019.)
theorem animorlr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wo ch ph) $;

--| Conjunction implies disjunction with one common formula (4/4). (Contributed by BJ, 4-Oct-2019.)
theorem animorrl (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wo ps ch) $;

--| Negated conjunction in terms of disjunction (De Morgan's law). Theorem *4.51 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.)
theorem ianor (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wa ph ps)) (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) $;

--| Conjunction in terms of disjunction (De Morgan's law). Theorem *4.5 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Nov-2012.)
theorem anor (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph ps) (wn (wo (wn ph) (wn ps))) $;

--| Negated disjunction in terms of conjunction (De Morgan's law). Compare Theorem *4.56 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem ioran (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wo ph ps)) (wa (wn ph) (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.52 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm4_52 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wn ps)) (wn (wo (wn ph) ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.53 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_53 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wa ph (wn ps))) (wo (wn ph) ps) $;

--| Theorem *4.54 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm4_54 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wn ph) ps) (wn (wo ph (wn ps))) $;

--| Theorem *4.55 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_55 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wa (wn ph) ps)) (wo ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.56 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_56 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wn ph) (wn ps)) (wn (wo ph ps)) $;

--| Disjunction in terms of conjunction (De Morgan's law). Compare Theorem *4.57 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem oran (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ps) (wn (wa (wn ph) (wn ps))) $;

--| Theorem *4.57 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_57 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wa (wn ph) (wn ps))) (wo ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *3.1 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wn (wo (wn ph) (wn ps))) $;

--| Theorem *3.11 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_11 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wo (wn ph) (wn ps))) (wa ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *3.12 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_12 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) (wa ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *3.13 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_13 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wn (wa ph ps)) (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *3.14 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_14 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wo (wn ph) (wn ps)) (wn (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.44 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_44 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wo ph (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.45 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_45 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ph (wo ph ps)) $;

--| Absorption of redundant internal disjunct. Compare Theorem *4.45 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Feb-2014.)
theorem orabs (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa (wo ph ps) ph) $;

--| Absorb a disjunct into a conjunct. (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 23-Jun-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 10-Nov-2013.)
theorem oranabs (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wo ph (wn ps)) ps) (wa ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *5.61 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 30-Jun-2013.)
theorem pm5_61 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wo ph ps) (wn ps)) (wa ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Conjunction in antecedent versus disjunction in consequent. Theorem *5.6 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jun-1994.)
theorem pm5_6 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ch) (wi ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Change disjunction in consequent to conjunction in antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jun-1994.)
theorem orcanai (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ch $;

--| Theorem *4.79 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 27-Jun-2013.)
theorem pm4_79 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wi ps ph) (wi ch ph)) (wi (wa ps ch) ph) $;

--| Theorem *5.53 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_53 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wo (wo ph ps) ch) th) (wa (wa (wi ph th) (wi ps th)) (wi ch th)) $;

--| Distributive law for disjunction. Theorem *4.41 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 5-Jan-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Nov-2013.)
theorem ordi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph (wa ps ch)) (wa (wo ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Distributive law for disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.)
theorem ordir (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) ch) (wa (wo ph ch) (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Distributive law for conjunction. Theorem *4.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jan-2013.)
theorem andi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wo ps ch)) (wo (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Distributive law for conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.)
theorem andir (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wo ph ps) ch) (wo (wa ph ch) (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Double distributive law for disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.)
theorem orddi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) (wa (wa (wo ph ch) (wo ph th)) (wa (wo ps ch) (wo ps th))) $;

--| Double distributive law for conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1994.)
theorem anddi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wo ph ps) (wo ch th)) (wo (wo (wa ph ch) (wa ph th)) (wo (wa ps ch) (wa ps th))) $;

--| Theorem *5.17 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm5_17 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wo ph ps) (wn (wa ph ps))) (wb ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.15 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 15-Oct-2013.)
theorem pm5_15 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wb ph ps) (wb ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.16 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 17-Oct-2013.)
theorem pm5_16 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wn (wa (wb ph ps) (wb ph (wn ps))) $;

--| Two ways to express exclusive disjunction ( ~ df-xor ). Theorem *5.22 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jan-2013.)
theorem xor (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wb ph ps)) (wo (wa ph (wn ps)) (wa ps (wn ph))) $;

--| Two ways to express "exclusive or". (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Jan-2013.)
theorem nbi2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wb ph ps)) (wa (wo ph ps) (wn (wa ph ps))) $;

--| Conjunction distributes over exclusive-or, using ` -. ( ph <-> ps ) ` to express exclusive-or. This is one way to interpret the distributive law of multiplication over addition in modulo 2 arithmetic. This is not necessarily true in intuitionistic logic, though ~ anxordi does hold in it. (Contributed by NM, 3-Oct-2008.)
theorem xordi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph (wn (wb ps ch))) (wn (wb (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch))) $;

--| Theorem *5.54 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Nov-2013.)
theorem pm5_54 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wb (wa ph ps) ph) (wb (wa ph ps) ps) $;

--| Theorem *5.62 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 21-Jun-2005.)
theorem pm5_62 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) (wn ps)) (wo ph (wn ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.63 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Dec-2012.)
theorem pm5_63 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wo ph ps) (wo ph (wa (wn ph) ps)) $;

--| Miscellaneous inference relating falsehoods. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-1994.)
theorem niabn (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi (wn ps) (wb (wa ch ps) (wn ph)) $;

--| Miscellaneous inference relating falsehoods. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-1994.)
theorem ninba (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi (wn ps) (wb (wn ph) (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.43 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 26-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm4_43 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa (wo ph ps) (wo ph (wn ps))) $;

--| Theorem *4.82 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_82 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wn ps))) (wn ph) $;

--| Theorem *4.83 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm4_83 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ps)) ps $;

--| Negation inferred from embedded conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Nov-2012.)
theorem pclem6 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph (wa ps (wn ph))) (wn ps) $;

--| Dijkstra-Scholten's Golden Rule for calculational proofs. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-2005.)
theorem bigolden (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb (wa ph ps) ph) (wb ps (wo ph ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 23-Jun-2005.)
theorem pm5_71 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps (wn ch)) (wb (wa (wo ph ps) ch) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *5.75 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Dec-2012.) (Proof shortened by Kyle Wyonch, 12-Feb-2021.)
theorem pm5_75 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ch (wn ps)) (wb ph (wo ps ch))) (wb (wa ph (wn ps)) ch) $;

--| Deduction for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Sep-2024.)
theorem ecase2d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wa ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wa ps th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ta (wo ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Obsolete version of ~ ecase2d as of 19-Sep-2024. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Dec-2012.) (New usage is discouraged.) (Proof modification is discouraged.)
theorem ecase2dOLD (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wa ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wa ps th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo ta (wo ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Inference for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 23-Mar-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 26-Nov-2012.)
theorem ecase3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi (wn (wo ph ps)) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Inference for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 13-Jul-2005.)
theorem ecase (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) ch $ >
  $ wi (wn ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Deduction for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 2-May-1996.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem ecase3d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wn (wo ps ch)) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Deduction for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-2012.)
theorem ecased (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wn ps) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wn ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Deduction for elimination by cases. (Contributed by NM, 24-May-2013.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Sep-2024.)
theorem ecase3ad (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wn ps) (wn ch)) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Obsolete version of ~ ecase3ad as of 20-Sep-2024. (Contributed by NM, 24-May-2013.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem ecase3adOLD (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wn ps) (wn ch)) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Inference for combining cases. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Jan-2013.)
theorem ccase (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ch ps) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ch th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wo ph ch) (wo ps th)) ta $;

--| Deduction for combining cases. (Contributed by NM, 9-May-2004.)
theorem ccased (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ch) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ta) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ta) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wo ps th) (wo ch ta)) et) $;

--| Inference for combining cases. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.)
theorem ccase2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ta $ >
  $ wi ch ta $ >
  $ wi th ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wo ph ch) (wo ps th)) ta $;

--| Inference eliminating two antecedents from the four possible cases that result from their true/false combinations. (Contributed by NM, 25-Oct-2003.)
theorem _4cases (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wn ph) ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wn ph) (wn ps)) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Deduction eliminating two antecedents from the four possible cases that result from their true/false combinations. (Contributed by NM, 19-Mar-2013.)
theorem _4casesdan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps (wn ch))) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wn ps) ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wn ps) (wn ch))) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Case disjunction according to the value of ` ph ` . (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-2019.)
theorem cases (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wb ps (wo (wa ph ch) (wa (wn ph) th)) $;

--| Lemma for an alternate version of weak deduction theorem. (Contributed by NM, 2-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Dec-2012.)
theorem dedlem0a (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wi (wi ch ph) (wa ps ph))) $;

--| Lemma for an alternate version of weak deduction theorem. (Contributed by NM, 2-Apr-1994.)
theorem dedlem0b (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb ps (wi (wi ps ph) (wa ch ph))) $;

--| Lemma for weak deduction theorem. See also ~ ifptru . (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2002.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem dedlema (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wo (wa ps ph) (wa ch (wn ph)))) $;

--| Lemma for weak deduction theorem. See also ~ ifpfal . (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem dedlemb (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb ch (wo (wa ps ph) (wa ch (wn ph)))) $;

--| Case disjunction according to the value of ` ph ` . (Contributed by BJ, 6-Apr-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Feb-2022.)
theorem cases2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) ch)) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| Alternate proof of ~ cases2 , not using ~ dedlema or ~ dedlemb . (Contributed by BJ, 6-Apr-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 2-Jan-2020.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem cases2ALT (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) ch)) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| An alternate definition of the biconditional. Theorem *5.23 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jun-2002.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Nov-2013.) (Proof shortened by NM, 29-Oct-2021.)
theorem dfbi3 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb ph ps) (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) (wn ps))) $;

--| Theorem *5.24 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 124. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_24 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) (wn ps)))) (wo (wa ph (wn ps)) (wa ps (wn ph))) $;

--| The disjunction of the four possible combinations of two wffs and their negations is always true. A four-way excluded middle (see ~ exmid ). (Contributed by David Abernethy, 28-Jan-2014.) (Proof shortened by NM, 29-Oct-2021.)
theorem _4exmid (ph ps: wff):
  $ wo (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) (wn ps))) (wo (wa ph (wn ps)) (wa ps (wn ph))) $;

--| The consensus theorem. This theorem and its dual (with ` \/ ` and ` /\ ` interchanged) are commonly used in computer logic design to eliminate redundant terms from Boolean expressions. Specifically, we prove that the term ` ( ps /\ ch ) ` on the left-hand side is redundant. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-2003.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Jan-2013.)
theorem consensus (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) ch)) (wa ps ch)) (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| Theorem *4.42 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. See also ~ ifpid . (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 21-Jun-2005.)
theorem pm4_42 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wo (wa ph ps) (wa ph (wn ps))) $;

--| A specialized lemma for set theory (to derive the Axiom of Pairing). (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-1995.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jan-2013.)
theorem prlem1 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb et ch) $ >
  $ wi ps (wn th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi (wo (wa ps ch) (wa th ta)) et)) $;

--| A specialized lemma for set theory (to derive the Axiom of Pairing). (Contributed by NM, 21-Jun-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 9-Dec-2012.)
theorem prlem2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wo (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) (wa (wo ph ch) (wo (wa ph ps) (wa ch th))) $;

--| A specialized lemma for set theory (ordered pair theorem). (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 8-Dec-2012.)
theorem oplem1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wo ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wo th ta) $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wi ch (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| A single axiom for Boolean algebra known as DN_1. See McCune, Veroff, Fitelson, Harris, Feist, Wos, _Short single axioms for Boolean algebra_, Journal of Automated Reasoning, 29(1):1--16, 2002. ( ~ https://www.cs.unm.edu/~~mccune/papers/basax/v12.pdf ). (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 3-Jul-2009.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Jan-2013.)
theorem dn1 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wn (wo (wn (wo (wn (wo ph ps)) ch)) (wn (wo ph (wn (wo (wn ch) (wn (wo ch th)))))))) ch $;

--| A closed form of ~ mpbir , analogous to ~ pm2.27 (assertion). (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (Proof shortened by Roger Witte, 17-Aug-2020.)
theorem bianir (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wb ps ph)) ps $;

--| Inference removing a negated conjunct in a disjunction of an antecedent if this conjunct is part of the disjunction. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 3-Nov-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Sep-2018.)
theorem jaoi2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wo ph (wa (wn ph) ch)) ps $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ch) ps $;

--| Inference separating a disjunct of an antecedent. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 25-May-2018.)
theorem jaoi3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa (wn ph) ch) ps $ >
  $ wi (wo ph ch) ps $;

--| Selecting one statement from a disjunction if one of the disjuncted statements is false. (Contributed by AV, 6-Sep-2018.) (Proof shortened by AV, 13-Oct-2018.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Jan-2020.)
theorem ornld (ph th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wi ph (wo th ta)) (wn th)) ta) $;

--| Extend wff notation to include the conditional operator for propositions.
term wif (ph ps ch: wff): wff;

--| Definition of the conditional operator for propositions. The expression ` if- ( ph , ps , ch ) ` is read "if ` ph ` then ` ps ` else ` ch ` ". See ~ dfifp2 , ~ dfifp3 , ~ dfifp4 , ~ dfifp5 , ~ dfifp6 and ~ dfifp7 for alternate definitions. This definition (in the form of ~ dfifp2 ) appears in Section II.24 of [Church] p. 129 (Definition D12 page 132), where it is called "conditioned disjunction". Church's ` [ ps , ph , ch ] ` corresponds to our ` if- ( ph , ps , ch ) ` (note the permutation of the first two variables). This form was chosen as the definition rather than ~ dfifp2 for compatibility with intuitionistic logic development: with this form, it is clear that ` if- ( ph , ps , ch ) ` implies decidability of ` ph ` , which is most often what is wanted. Church uses the conditional operator as an intermediate step to prove completeness of some systems of connectives. The first result is that the system ` { if- , T. , F. } ` is complete: for the induction step, consider a formula of n+1 variables; single out one variable, say ` ph ` ; when one sets ` ph ` to True (resp. False), then what remains is a formula of n variables, so by the induction hypothesis it is equivalent to a formula using only the connectives ` if- , T. , F. ` , say ` ps ` (resp. ` ch ` ); therefore, the formula ` if- ( ph , ps , ch ) ` is equivalent to the initial formula of n+1 variables. Now, since ` { -> , -. } ` and similar systems suffice to express the connectives ` if- , T. , F. ` , they are also complete. (Contributed by BJ, 22-Jun-2019.)
axiom df_ifp (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wo (wa ph ps) (wa (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. The value of ` if- ( ph , ps , ch ) ` is "if ` ph ` then ` ps ` , and if not ` ph ` then ` ch ` ". This is the definition used in Section II.24 of [Church] p. 129 (Definition D12 page 132) (see comment of ~ df-ifp ). (Contributed by BJ, 22-Jun-2019.)
theorem dfifp2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.)
theorem dfifp3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wa (wi ph ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.)
theorem dfifp4 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wa (wo (wn ph) ps) (wo ph ch)) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by BJ, 2-Oct-2019.)
theorem dfifp5 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wa (wo (wn ph) ps) (wi (wn ph) ch)) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by BJ, 2-Oct-2019.)
theorem dfifp6 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wo (wa ph ps) (wn (wi ch ph))) $;

--| Alternate definition of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by BJ, 2-Oct-2019.)
theorem dfifp7 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wi (wi ch ph) (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Define the biconditional as conditional logic operator. (Contributed by RP, 20-Apr-2020.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 30-Apr-2024.)
theorem ifpdfbi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb ph ps) (wif ph ps (wn ps)) $;

--| The conditional operator is implied by the conjunction of its possible outputs. Dual statement of ~ ifpor . (Contributed by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.)
theorem anifp (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ps ch) (wif ph ps ch) $;

--| The conditional operator implies the disjunction of its possible outputs. Dual statement of ~ anifp . (Contributed by BJ, 1-Oct-2019.)
theorem ifpor (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wif ph ps ch) (wo ps ch) $;

--| Conditional operator for the negation of a proposition. (Contributed by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-May-2024.)
theorem ifpn (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wif (wn ph) ch ps) $;

--| Obsolete version of ~ ifpn as of 5-May-2024. (Contributed by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem ifpnOLD (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ch) (wif (wn ph) ch ps) $;

--| Value of the conditional operator for propositions when its first argument is true. Analogue for propositions of ~ iftrue . This is essentially ~ dedlema . (Contributed by BJ, 20-Sep-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 10-Jul-2020.)
theorem ifptru (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb (wif ph ps ch) ps) $;

--| Value of the conditional operator for propositions when its first argument is false. Analogue for propositions of ~ iffalse . This is essentially ~ dedlemb . (Contributed by BJ, 20-Sep-2019.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jun-2020.)
theorem ifpfal (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb (wif ph ps ch) ch) $;

--| Value of the conditional operator for propositions when the same proposition is returned in either case. Analogue for propositions of ~ ifid . This is essentially ~ pm4.42 . (Contributed by BJ, 20-Sep-2019.)
theorem ifpid (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wif ph ps ps) ps $;

--| Version of ~ cases expressed using ` if- ` . Case disjunction according to the value of ` ph ` . One can see this as a proof that the two hypotheses characterize the conditional operator for propositions. For the converses, see ~ ifptru and ~ ifpfal . (Contributed by BJ, 20-Sep-2019.)
theorem casesifp (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wn ph) (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wb ps (wif ph ch th) $;

--| Equivalence deduction for conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by AV, 30-Dec-2020.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 17-Apr-2024.)
theorem ifpbi123d (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ze) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wif ps ch th) (wif ta et ze)) $;

--| Obsolete version of ~ ifpbi123d as of 17-Apr-2024. (Contributed by AV, 30-Dec-2020.) (New usage is discouraged.) (Proof modification is discouraged.)
theorem ifpbi123dOLD (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ze) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wif ps ch th) (wif ta et ze)) $;

--| Equivalence deduction for conditional operator for propositions. Convenience theorem for a frequent case. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 28-Apr-2024.)
theorem ifpbi23d (ph ps ch th et ze: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ch et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ze) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wif ps ch th) (wif ps et ze)) $;

--| Separation of the values of the conditional operator for propositions. (Contributed by AV, 30-Dec-2020.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 27-Feb-2021.)
theorem ifpimpda (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wn ps)) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wif ps ch th) $;

--| The value of the conditional operator for propositions is its third argument if the first and second argument imply the third argument. (Contributed by AV, 4-Apr-2021.)
theorem _1fpid3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wif ph ps ch) ch $;

--| Hypothesis builder for the weak deduction theorem. For more information, see the Weak Deduction Theorem page ~ mmdeduction.html . (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2002.) Revised to use the conditional operator. (Revised by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.) Commute consequent. (Revised by Steven Nguyen, 27-Apr-2023.)
theorem elimh (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wb (wif ch ph ps) ph) (wb ta ch) $ >
  $ wi (wb (wif ch ph ps) ps) (wb ta th) $ >
  $ th $ >
  $ ta $;

--| The weak deduction theorem. For more information, see the Weak Deduction Theorem page ~ mmdeduction.html . (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2002.) Revised to use the conditional operator. (Revised by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.) Commute consequent. (Revised by Steven Nguyen, 27-Apr-2023.)
theorem dedt (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wb (wif ch ph ps) ph) (wb ta th) $ >
  $ ta $ >
  $ wi ch th $;

--| Proof of ~ con3 from its associated inference ~ con3i that illustrates the use of the weak deduction theorem ~ dedt . (Contributed by NM, 27-Jun-2002.) Revised to use the conditional operator. (Revised by BJ, 30-Sep-2019.) Revised ~ dedt and ~ elimh . (Revised by Steven Nguyen, 27-Apr-2023.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem con3ALT (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wn ps) (wn ph)) $;

--| Extend wff definition to include three-way disjunction ('or').
term w3o (ph ps ch: wff): wff;

--| Extend wff definition to include three-way conjunction ('and').
term w3a (ph ps ch: wff): wff;

--| Define disjunction ('or') of three wff's. Definition *2.33 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 105. This abbreviation reduces the number of parentheses and emphasizes that the order of bracketing is not important by virtue of the associative law ~ orass . (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.)
axiom df_3or (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (wo (wo ph ps) ch) $;

--| Define conjunction ('and') of three wff's. Definition *4.34 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. This abbreviation reduces the number of parentheses and emphasizes that the order of bracketing is not important by virtue of the associative law ~ anass . (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.)
axiom df_3an (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa (wa ph ps) ch) $;

--| Associative law for triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3orass (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (wo ph (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Partial elimination of a triple disjunction by denial of a disjunct. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 26-Mar-2011.)
theorem _3orel1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wn ph) (wi (w3o ph ps ch) (wo ps ch)) $;

--| Rotation law for triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3orrot (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (w3o ps ch ph) $;

--| Commutation law for triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-Sep-2016.)
theorem _3orcoma (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (w3o ps ph ch) $;

--| Commutation law for triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 20-Apr-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 8-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3orcomb (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (w3o ph ch ps) $;

--| Associative law for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3anass (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Convert triple conjunction to conjunction, then commute. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 14-Jun-2011.) (Revised to shorten ~ 3ancoma by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3anan12 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa ps (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Convert triple conjunction to conjunction, then commute. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3anan32 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa (wa ph ch) ps) $;

--| Commutation law for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 5-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3ancoma (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (w3a ps ph ch) $;

--| Commutation law for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Revised to shorten ~ 3anrot by Wolf Lammen, 9-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3ancomb (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (w3a ph ch ps) $;

--| Rotation law for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 9-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3anrot (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (w3a ps ch ph) $;

--| Reversal law for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3anrev (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (w3a ch ps ph) $;

--| Distribution of triple conjunction over conjunction. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 4-Nov-2018.)
theorem anandi3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Distribution of triple conjunction over conjunction. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 4-Nov-2018.)
theorem anandi3r (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Idempotent law for conjunction. (Contributed by Peter Mazsa, 17-Oct-2023.)
theorem _3anidm (ph: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ph ph) ph $;

--| Associative law for four conjunctions with a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 24-Jun-2018.)
theorem _3an4anass (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wa (w3a ph ps ch) th) (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) $;

--| Negated triple disjunction as triple conjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 19-Apr-2011.)
theorem _3ioran (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wn (w3o ph ps ch)) (w3a (wn ph) (wn ps) (wn ch)) $;

--| Negated triple conjunction expressed in terms of triple disjunction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 15-Aug-2009.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Revised by Wolf Lammen, 8-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3ianor (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wn (w3a ph ps ch)) (w3o (wn ph) (wn ps) (wn ch)) $;

--| Triple conjunction expressed in terms of triple disjunction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 15-Aug-2009.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 8-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3anor (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3a ph ps ch) (wn (w3o (wn ph) (wn ps) (wn ch))) $;

--| Triple disjunction in terms of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-2012.)
theorem _3oran (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (w3o ph ps ch) (wn (w3a (wn ph) (wn ps) (wn ch))) $;

--| Importation from double to triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1995.) (Revised to shorten ~ 3imp by Wolf Lammen, 20-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3impa (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| Importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3imp (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| The importation inference ~ 3imp with commutation of the first and third conjuncts of the assertion relative to the hypothesis. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 11-Sep-2016.)
theorem _3imp31 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ch ps ph) th $;

--| Importation inference. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.)
theorem _3imp231 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch ph) th $;

--| The importation inference ~ 3imp with commutation of the first and second conjuncts of the assertion relative to the hypothesis. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 11-Sep-2016.) (Revised to shorten ~ 3com12 by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3imp21 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ph ch) th $;

--| Importation from double to triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1995.)
theorem _3impb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| Importation to triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 13-Jun-2006.)
theorem _3impib (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| Importation to triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 13-Jun-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3impia (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| Exportation from triple to double conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1995.) (Revised to shorten ~ 3exp and ~ pm3.2an3 by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3expa (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $;

--| Exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 30-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3exp (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $;

--| Exportation from triple to double conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1995.)
theorem _3expb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $;

--| Exportation from triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 19-May-2007.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3expia (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $;

--| Exportation from triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 19-May-2007.)
theorem _3expib (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $;

--| Commutation in antecedent. Swap 1st and 2nd. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3com12 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ph ch) th $;

--| Commutation in antecedent. Swap 1st and 3rd. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3com13 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ch ps ph) th $;

--| Commutation in antecedent. Rotate right. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.) (Revised by Wolf Lammen, 9-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3comr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ch ph ps) th $;

--| Commutation in antecedent. Swap 2nd and 3rd. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 9-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3com23 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ps) th $;

--| Commutation in antecedent. Rotate left. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.)
theorem _3coml (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch ph) th $;

--| Join consequents with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 9-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3jca (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a ps ch th) $;

--| Deduction conjoining the consequents of three implications. (Contributed by NM, 25-Sep-2005.)
theorem _3jcad (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (w3a ch th ta)) $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jul-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant1 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a th ph ps) ch $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jul-1995.)
theorem _3adant2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph th ps) ch $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 16-Jul-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant3 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps th) ch $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3ad2ant1 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps th) ch $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3ad2ant2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ph th) ch $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3ad2ant3 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps th ph) ch $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem simp1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) ph $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem simp2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) ps $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Jun-2022.)
theorem simp3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) ch $;

--| Infer a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 19-Apr-2005.)
theorem simp1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ w3a ph ps ch $ >
  $ ph $;

--| Infer a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 19-Apr-2005.)
theorem simp2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ w3a ph ps ch $ >
  $ ps $;

--| Infer a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 19-Apr-2005.)
theorem simp3i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ w3a ph ps ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Sep-2005.)
theorem simp1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Sep-2005.)
theorem simp2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Sep-2005.)
theorem simp3d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem simp1bi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem simp2bi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Deduce a conjunct from a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem simp3bi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3simpa (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wa ph ps) $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3simpb (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wa ph ch) $;

--| Simplification of triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3simpc (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wa ps ch) $;

--| Join antecedents and consequents with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3anim123i (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ta et $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ta) (w3a ps th et) $;

--| Add two conjuncts to antecedent and consequent. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 16-Aug-2009.)
theorem _3anim1i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch th) (w3a ps ch th) $;

--| Add two conjuncts to antecedent and consequent. (Contributed by AV, 21-Nov-2019.)
theorem _3anim2i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (w3a ch ph th) (w3a ch ps th) $;

--| Add two conjuncts to antecedent and consequent. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 19-Aug-2009.)
theorem _3anim3i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (w3a ch th ph) (w3a ch th ps) $;

--| Join 3 biconditionals with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3anbi123i (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb ta et $ >
  $ wb (w3a ph ch ta) (w3a ps th et) $;

--| Join 3 biconditionals with disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 17-May-1994.)
theorem _3orbi123i (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb ta et $ >
  $ wb (w3o ph ch ta) (w3o ps th et) $;

--| Inference adding two conjuncts to each side of a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 8-Sep-2006.)
theorem _3anbi1i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (w3a ph ch th) (w3a ps ch th) $;

--| Inference adding two conjuncts to each side of a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 8-Sep-2006.)
theorem _3anbi2i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (w3a ch ph th) (w3a ch ps th) $;

--| Inference adding two conjuncts to each side of a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 8-Sep-2006.)
theorem _3anbi3i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (w3a ch th ph) (w3a ch th ps) $;

--| A triple syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 13-May-2004.)
theorem syl3an (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ta et $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps th et) ze $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ta) ze $;

--| A triple syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 15-Oct-2005.)
theorem syl3anb (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb ta et $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps th et) ze $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ta) ze $;

--| A triple syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 29-Dec-2011.)
theorem syl3anbr (ph ps ch th ta et ze: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wb th ch $ >
  $ wb et ta $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps th et) ze $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ta) ze $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 22-Aug-1995.)
theorem syl3an1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch th) ta $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch th) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 22-Aug-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 26-Jun-2022.)
theorem syl3an2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch th) ta $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ph th) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 22-Aug-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 26-Jun-2022.)
theorem syl3an3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch th) ta $ >
  $ wi (w3a ps ch ph) ta $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ta ph ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ta ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ta ps ch)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ta ch)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch ta)) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad4ant123 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) ta) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad4ant124 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad4ant134 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ta) ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad4ant234 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ta ph) ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant1l (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa ta ph) ps ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant1r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a (wa ph ta) ps ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant2l (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wa ta ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant2r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph (wa ps ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant3l (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps (wa ta ch)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Jun-2022.)
theorem _3adant3r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
