--| Remove a hypothesis from the second member of a biconditional. (Contributed by FL, 22-Jul-2008.)
theorem _3anibar (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wb th (wa ch ta)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wb th ta) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ph ps ch) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ph ch) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ch ph) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ph ps ch $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ps ph ch $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix3i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ps ch ph $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ch th) $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ch ps th) $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix3d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ch th ps) $;

--| Infer conjunction of premises. (Contributed by NM, 10-Feb-1995.)
theorem _3pm3_2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ w3a ph ps ch $;

--| Version of ~ pm3.2 for a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 24-Oct-2011.) (Proof shortened by Kyle Wyonch, 24-Apr-2021.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Jun-2022.)
theorem pm3_2an3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (w3a ph ps ch))) $;

--| Detach a conjunction of truths in a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-2011.)
theorem mpbir3an (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ th $ >
  $ wb ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ ph $;

--| Detach a conjunction of truths in a biconditional. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-May-2014.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 9-Jan-2015.)
theorem mpbir3and (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps (w3a ch th ta)) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Syllogism inference. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-May-2014.)
theorem syl3anbrc (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wb ta (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Syllogism inference. (Contributed by Peter Mazsa, 18-Sep-2022.)
theorem syl21anbrc (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wb ta (wa (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| An elimination deduction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3imp3i2an (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa th ta) et $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) et $;

--| Apply ~ ex to a hypothesis with a 3-right-nested conjunction antecedent, with the antecedent of the assertion being a triple conjunction rather than a 2-right-nested conjunction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 22-Apr-2018.)
theorem ex3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wi th ta) $;

--| Importation to left triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3imp1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ch) th) ta $;

--| Importation deduction for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-2006.)
theorem _3impd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (w3a ps ch th) ta) $;

--| Importation to right triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-2006.)
theorem _3imp2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch th)) ta $;

--| Importation inference (undistribute conjunction). (Contributed by NM, 14-Aug-1995.)
theorem _3impdi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $;

--| Importation inference (undistribute conjunction). (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1995.)
theorem _3impdir (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch ps)) th $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ch ps) th $;

--| Exportation from left triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3exp1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| Exportation deduction for triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-2006.)
theorem _3expd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (w3a ps ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| Exportation from right triple conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-2006.)
theorem _3exp2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| A triple exportation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 8-Jul-2009.)
theorem exp5o (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wi (wa th ta) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $;

--| A triple exportation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 8-Jul-2009.)
theorem exp516 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (w3a ps ch th)) ta) et $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $;

--| A triple exportation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 8-Jul-2009.)
theorem exp520 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ch) (wa th ta)) et $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $;

--| Version of ~ impexp for a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 31-Dec-2011.)
theorem _3impexp (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb (wi (w3a ph ps ch) th) (wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th))) $;

--| Swap conjuncts. (Contributed by NM, 16-Dec-2007.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem _3an1rs (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps th) ch) ta $;

--| Associative law for conjunction applied to antecedent (eliminates syllogism). (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 4-Jan-2017.)
theorem _3anassrs (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th) ta $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad5ant245 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wa ta ph) et) ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 17-Oct-2017.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2022.)
theorem ad5ant234 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
